proposed_schema_examples:
Canonical function manifest fragment:
{
  "name": "createInvoice",
  "params": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "customer_id": {"type": "string"},
      "items": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object"}},
      "metadata": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": true}
    },
    "required": ["customer_id", "items"]
  },
  "compat": {
    "min_version": 1,
    "aliases": {"acct_id": "customer_id"},
    "partial_apply": true
  }
}

Example request that relies on partial-apply (missing metadata block):
{
  "customer_id": "cust_123",
  "items": []
}
Server binds defaults for "metadata" and returns diagnostics with PC_PARTIAL_APPLY

Diagnostics envelope example (transport-level):
{
  "diagnostics": [
    {"code": "PC_PARTIAL_APPLY", "path": "/metadata", "message": "metadata injected from defaults (source=server-cache)"},
    {"code": "PC_DEPRECATED_ALIASED", "path": "/acct_id", "message": "acct_id mapped to customer_id via alias table"}
  ],
  "canonicalized_params": {"customer_id": "cust_123", "items": [], "metadata": {}}
}
